Flip `if (step <= cnt)` to `if (step < cnt)` in sh4_timer_tick() (dev_sh4.c:231).

step == cnt is the single input where the two arms of the tick swap.  Under the mutant it
takes the underflow arm with remaining = (uint64_t)cnt - cnt - 1 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, so TCNT
lands on 00001fa6/UNF1 instead of 00000000/UNF0 -- wrong value AND a spurious underflow flag.

MEASURED: exactly ONE row of sixteen goes red, and it is the row written for this boundary --
`step == cnt (boundary)`, whose own comment says "the step == cnt case is the one the
comparison itself turns on, so it is asserted rather than approached from one side".  Every
other row is byte-identical between the arms: both multi-period rows, the three-timer row, the
interrupt row, the stopped-timer row and the 70000-call freeze row.  So this mutant certifies
that row and nothing else, which is what the pin claims.

It is the edit a maintainer might plausibly make in good faith, and the code's own comment at
dev_sh4.c:208-216 exists to refute it: TCNT counts TCOR..0 and underflows AFTER 0, so landing
exactly on 0 is not yet an underflow.  Read that as "reaching zero IS the underflow" and
`step < cnt` follows directly.  It is also the same off-by-one family as the defect #400 fixed,
which landed on TCOR-1 rather than TCOR.

DELIBERATELY NOT `period = (uint64_t)d->tcor[i] + 1` -> `(uint64_t)d->tcor[i]`, the other
obvious off-by-one.  With TCOR == 0 that makes period 0 and `remaining % period` at :237 is a
divide by zero; the `TCOR=0 steady state` row reaches it, so the mutant dies by SIGNAL 8 before
printing a verdict.  A crash is a FAULT, never a detection -- selfmutant.py's F5 scores it
SETUP, and footbridge.why records the same rejection for the same reason.  This mutant keeps
the host alive and fails on VALUES.

Also not a whole-branch revert: that reddens several rows at once and proves only that deleting
arithmetic breaks the tests of that arithmetic.

The row id is "boundary", which names exactly one row in the pristine table.  "step == cnt"
would have named TWO ("step == cnt (boundary)" and "step == cnt+1 -> TCOR") and selfmutant.py's
guard 5 reports that as SETUP; measured both ways before choosing.  No extra CC flags: the gate
builds this harness without -D_POSIX_C_SOURCE and without -I../src, and both arms were built
under BOTH flag sets and produced byte-identical output, so the self-mutant lane is not
compiling something else.
